 name←{space}GetItemName filename;extensions
⍝ Returns the APL name of whatever `filename` holds, or an empty vector in case it cannot be established.\\
⍝ A project is managed either by Link or by acre, never by both, therefore Link is asked first,
⍝ and acre is consulted only when Link does not know the file.\\
⍝ The optional `space` is the name of the project's namespace; acre needs it in order to
⍝ qualify the name it returns.
 space←{0<⎕NC ⍵:⍎⍵ ⋄ ''}'space'
 name←''
 extensions←ListOfDyalogFilesExtensions,'.charlist' '.charmat' '.charstring'
 :If 9=⎕SE.⎕NC'Link'
     name←⎕SE.Link.GetItemName filename
 :EndIf
 :If 0=≢name
 :AndIf (⊂⎕C 3⊃⎕NPARTS filename)∊extensions  ⍝ Cheap test first: it saves probing for acre
 :AndIf U.AcreIsAvailable
     name←space GetAcreItemName filename
 :EndIf
⍝Done
